WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.856
This is Ingot, the income and expense tracker inside EquityFoundry.

2
00:00:04.856 --> 00:00:13.129
In a few minutes you'll see how to add your rentals, log rent and bills, and have your Schedule E totals ready at tax time.

3
00:00:13.929 --> 00:00:15.402
Tap Ingot in the menu.

4
00:00:15.402 --> 00:00:17.545
On a phone, it's called Rentals.

5
00:00:17.545 --> 00:00:24.041
Your entries are saved on your device, and if you sign in, they stay in sync across your devices.

6
00:00:24.841 --> 00:00:27.432
Start on Properties and tap Add property.

7
00:00:27.432 --> 00:00:34.575
Give it a name and address, the number of units, the rent you expect each month, and the purchase price and date.

8
00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:38.494
Ingot uses the expected rent to show when rent comes in short.

9
00:00:40.151 --> 00:00:42.801
Quick add is how you log money in or out.

10
00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:44.158
There are four kinds.

11
00:00:44.158 --> 00:00:45.321
Income, like rent.

12
00:00:45.321 --> 00:00:48.165
Expenses, the costs of running the property.

13
00:00:48.165 --> 00:00:52.754
Distributions, money you take out, which never lowers your tax numbers.

14
00:00:52.754 --> 00:00:56.891
And other, for things like loan principal and deposits you hold.

15
00:00:56.891 --> 00:00:58.959
Here's November rent for Unit A:

16
00:00:58.959 --> 00:01:01.868
amount, date, property, category, and a note.

17
00:01:02.668 --> 00:01:05.848
For a mortgage payment, pick mortgage interest.

18
00:01:05.848 --> 00:01:11.599
Only the interest is a Schedule E expense, so type the principal part in its own box.

19
00:01:11.599 --> 00:01:14.508
Ingot logs it separately as loan principal.

20
00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:16.999
Repairs work the same way.

21
00:01:16.999 --> 00:01:22.333
Pick the property and the category, add a note, and attach a photo of the receipt.

22
00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:24.609
On a phone, this opens your camera.

23
00:01:26.735 --> 00:01:35.176
The dashboard shows income, expenses, net and distributions for this month, the quarter, the year to date, or the last twelve months.

24
00:01:35.176 --> 00:01:44.633
Below that, income against expenses by month, your biggest costs, and how each property compares, including rent collected against what you expected.

25
00:01:45.433 --> 00:01:48.155
Month view lists every entry for one month.

26
00:01:48.155 --> 00:01:55.119
Step back and forward with the arrows, filter to one property, and tap an entry to edit it or see its receipt.

27
00:01:55.919 --> 00:01:57.733
At tax time, open Taxes.

28
00:01:57.733 --> 00:02:05.975
Ingot totals each property on the Schedule E lines, from rents received to total expenses and income or loss.

29
00:02:05.975 --> 00:02:09.907
Download it as a CSV or a PDF for your tax preparer.

30
00:02:09.907 --> 00:02:14.671
It's not tax advice, so have your preparer confirm the numbers.

31
00:02:15.471 --> 00:02:18.885
The maintenance log keeps a record of every repair:

32
00:02:18.885 --> 00:02:20.960
the vendor, the cost and notes.

33
00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:25.110
Leave the box ticked to log the cost as a repairs expense too.

34
00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:29.060
Untick it if you already logged the payment, like this one.

35
00:02:31.001 --> 00:02:33.778
Already have it all in your bank account?

36
00:02:33.778 --> 00:02:37.572
Download the transactions as a CSV and import them here.

37
00:02:37.572 --> 00:02:43.941
Map the columns once, tag each row to a property and category, and Ingot remembers your rules.

38
00:02:43.941 --> 00:02:48.345
Rows you've imported before are flagged, so nothing counts twice.

39
00:02:49.145 --> 00:02:58.426
The free version tracks one property for the current year, with quick add, the dashboard totals, month view, and your Schedule E totals on screen.

40
00:02:58.426 --> 00:03:07.961
Pro adds unlimited properties, the charts and property table, receipt photos, past years, Schedule E downloads, the maintenance log, and bank imports.

41
00:03:08.761 --> 00:03:09.730
That's Ingot.

42
00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:13.384
Log it as it happens, and tax time takes minutes.

43
00:03:13.384 --> 00:03:17.486
Try it at octo pie sees labs dot com slash rental calc.
